26011:{s:"Organon",e:"Stuart Close defined the Second best remedy as the one that most nearly covers the totality when the simillimum cannot be found."},
26012:{s:"Organon",e:"Doctrine of Drug Individuality states every medicine has unique, peculiar actions not produced identically by any other substance."},
26013:{s:"Organon",e:"Chronological order in 6th edition: Dynamic neutralization (§26fn) → First rudiments of MM (§108fn) → Quidquid in buccam venit (§141fn) → Antitype (§274fn) → Intermediate remedy (§283fn)."},
26014:{s:"Organon",e:"Alternating diseases are chronic diseases where two or more miasmatic disease states alternate their dominance in symptom expression."},
